<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Florent of Hainaut</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1255–1297</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Florent of Hainaut was a Flemish nobleman who became prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> in 1289 by marrying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isabella-of-villehardouin">Isabella of Villehardouin</a>. He made a truce with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> that brought several years of peace and prosperity to the principality, and he was the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matilda-of-hainaut">Matilda of Hainaut</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/florent-of-hainaut.jpg" alt="Florent of Hainaut" width="320" height="290" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Schlumberger, Gustave Léon, 1844-1929 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Florent_of_Hainaut.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
